# tally 2.2.1, E §11 REQ-CLOCK: "a cut an ask's literal states after `on` (`as known`, `with known`; a literal in `( )`
# too), in an ask load left standing" refuses the request, the run's one result, exit 1.
# S-233.8: `as known (2026-06-01)` after on 2026-03-01. tally 2.2 answered it alone, RUN-DOMAIN.
=== options exit=1
=== b.tally
model bob
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "b card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input pay: money PLN

def twice: money PLN = pay + pay at reader

ask q: twice law 2026-03-01

ask qc: twice law 2026-03-01 as known (2026-06-01)

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 3 000.00 PLN "the card"
=== expect
refused: REQ-CLOCK as known 2026-06-01 is after the model's on 2026-03-01
